      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Identify the surface $4{y}^{2}+8y+9{z}^{2}-5x+9=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square in the $y$ term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}+8y+9{z}^{2}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ 4({y}^{2}+2y)+9{z}^{2}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ 4[(y+1)^{2}-1]+9{z}^{2}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ 4(y+1)^{2}-4+9{z}^{2}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ 4(y+1)^{2}+9{z}^{2}-5x+5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(y+1)^{2}+9{z}^{2}-5x+5 & =0 \\\\ 4(y+1)^{2}+9{z}^{2} & =5(x-1) \\\\ \\frac{4(y+1)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{9{z}^{2}}{5} & =x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an elliptic paraboloid centered at $(1,-1,0).$",
